        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): make mobile pairing easy to find",
        "body": "Closes #100154\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nUsers pairing the iOS app could miss the supported web flow because its only trigger was inside the Devices card near the bottom of Nodes. Searching the main UI or Settings gave no obvious route to the QR setup dialog.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a subtle phone action to the persistent sidebar footer and a Mobile app action to Quick Settings. All three entry points, including the existing Nodes button, now share one app-level dialog state; setup-code cancellation and pending-request refreshes remain synchronized across Gateway reconnects and pairing events.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators with administrator access can open mobile pairing directly from any Control UI page or from Quick Settings, scan the QR code, and jump to Nodes to manage requests. Non-admin operators see the actions disabled with the existing access explanation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run ui/src/pages/config/quick.test.ts ui/src/pages/nodes/view.devices.test.ts ui/src/lib/device-pair-setup.test.ts` — 23 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/mobile-pairing.e2e.test.ts` — browser E2E passed for sidebar open, Quick Settings open, QR rendering, live pending-request refresh, code regeneration, and Manage devices routing.\n- `pnpm ui:build` — production Control UI build passed.\n- `check:changed` — Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwr1yvdny7vpvg21qtcvqvjq`, exit 0; typechecks, lint, import-cycle, and pairing guards passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28727067161\n- Structured Codex autoreview — accepted one pending-count synchronization finding, fixed it, reran focused proof, then clean with no actionable findings.\n- Visual proof captured in the attached-Chrome mocked Control UI; screenshots are attached to this PR.\n\nAI-assisted: implemented and reviewed with Codex; maintainer understands the code and proof above.\n",
